00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:22.050
The boy raced through the
woods, blood streaming

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:26.170
from his hand, he was growing
faint, can't pass out,

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.580
just gotta make it to the fence.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.240
He heard his pursuers yelling,

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.253
they sounded as panicked as he felt.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.450
He didn't know if the
dizziness was due to blood loss

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.250
or the shock of what had just happened.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.140
They were gonna kill me.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:41.360
He had know this place
was twisted from day one

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.730
when they'd stripped him of everything,

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.370
including his own name,

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.650
but even with all the
vile things he'd seen.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.720
He had still assumed that
the brutal punishments

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.641
were designed to
intimidate, not exterminate.

00:04:51.641 --> 00:04:54.430
That's why he'd been so
calm, willingly letting them

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.600
guide him along blindfolded and gagged,

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.050
right up until the moment
they'd sliced his palm.

00:04:59.959 --> 00:05:02.600
What if this particular
test was no different,

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:04.810
maybe he was doing exactly
what they wanted him to,

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.730
running through the trees
like a trophy animal.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:10.120
They'd only cut his hand, no arteries,

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.810
plus he'd somehow gotten away
from the two men holding him,

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.050
one of them enormous, much
bigger than any of the other

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.008
adults he'd seen there,

00:05:17.008 --> 00:05:19.030
had they purposely let him go?

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.810
No, he shouldn't sell himself short,

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:21.910
he'd fought like hell.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.290
The boy felt a flash of pride,

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.860
all those hours of memorizing
Jean-Claude Van Damme,

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.500
his moves had been worth it.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.473
Can't wait to re-watch Kickboxer.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.130
He struggled to move at a full clip

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:37.450
as branches, rocks, and logs snuck up

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.280
on him in the sparse moonlight.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.290
He dodged the obstacles
hoping he was heading

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.760
in the right direction.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.113
Where's the damn fence?

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.300
He saw it just before he collided with it.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.310
The grass of the pasture on the other side

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.040
of the chain link's glowing a dull gray

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.173
under the night sky.

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.510
He started to climb without thinking,

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:56.560
pain exploding as the metal wire

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.600
slipped into his open
wound, he stifled a scream,

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.620
hoping to conceal his
exact point of escape.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.670
While clenching his jaw,
summoning the resolve

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:07.064
to hoist himself up the 10 foot barrier,

00:06:07.064 --> 00:06:09.540
he saw it, a cut section of fence

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.623
not five steps away, lucky.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:14.530
As he pushed his way through the flap

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:15.550
and stood in the pasture,

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.510
he heard the roar of
an engine to his left,

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.670
the pick up truck was hurtling

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.470
across the pasture in his direction.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.570
They were trying to head him off.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.900
He broke into a sprint
toward the cover of trees

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.760
bordering the pasture, his
shadows sprawling in front of him

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.750
as the headlight shined on his back.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.380
He was confident in his speed,

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:34.610
99th percentile in the
President's challenge

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:36.710
shuttle run, he'd timed himself.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.240
But they were closing the distance fast,

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:41.313
get to the tree line.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.000
He'd knew there would be
a barbed wire cow fence

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:45.960
at the edge of the field,

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.910
he'd have to clear it in stride.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:50.670
In only a matter of seconds
they would be upon him.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.210
He was steps from the trees,

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:53.870
the headlights lit up the short fence,

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.770
helping him judge his distance.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.780
He stutter stepped to set up his leap,

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.363
then threw his leg in
the air, a clean jump.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.610
He heard the truck skid
to a stop on the wet grass

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:06.474
behind him, the doors
opening, men screaming.

00:07:06.474 --> 00:07:08.506
He knew this stretch of forest well,

00:07:08.506 --> 00:07:11.030
there was barely a patch
of nature around town

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.350
he hadn't explored.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:15.680
Another 100 feet or so and
he's make it to the clearing.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:17.650
He broke into the lane
cut through the forest,

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.880
a grassy corridor that
followed the sewage line

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.290
along its lazy descent to
the water treatment plant.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.990
He heard the chasers clumsily
moving through the woods

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:29.853
crashing into branches and
crumbling to themselves, morons.

00:07:31.062 --> 00:07:33.150
Randomly choosing a direction, he dashed

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:36.400
down the clearing, reaching a
manhole in less than 50 steps.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.770
He grabbed a nearby stick
and jammed it into the notch

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.200
on the cover, just as he'd
done a thousand times before,

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.910
no longer thinking about
his throbbing hand.

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.610
The weighty metal disk lifted,

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.790
releasing an acrid smell.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.080
He raised the lid on his edge,

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.540
and swiftly descended into
the rank darkness below,

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:54.190
skittering down the iron
rungs, as fast as you could.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.290
The disheveled man popped out of the trees

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.940
no more than 10 seconds
after he had dropped

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:00.990
the manhole cover in place.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:04.230
The boy listened as their
cursing voices passed them.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:07.053
He waited in stinking silence
for another five minutes.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:11.120
Thrusting open the cover, he
emerged into the damp air,

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:13.053
the boy fled deeper into the woods.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.545
And we're off to the races!

