So I'll just read through this.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:41.053
Chapter 10, right at the top.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.460
Rex and Leaf walked into the cafeteria

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:48.030
on their first day at
Bleak Creek High School.

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:51.610
This moment had been building
in Rex's mind for years,

00:19:51.610 --> 00:19:54.390
ever since his older
sister Misty told him that

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:56.840
whoever you sat with
at lunch that first day

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:59.170
could determine your future.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:01.590
Brad Stewart was the
smartest guy in eighth grade,

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:04.730
she said, but he sat with
the Gardner twins his

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:07.813
freshman year and now he
drives an ice cream truck.

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:12.940
He, Leaf, and Alecia had developed a plan.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.020
Instead of buying lunch,
they would bring their own

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.830
to avoid the hiccup of having
to go through the line.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:20.980
Then they'd take their own brown bags,

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:23.040
lunch boxes were strictly off limits,

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:26.170
a sacrifice particularly
challenging for Leaf,

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:29.070
directly to the spot of
their choice, sit down,

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:32.340
and wait to see who naturally joined them.

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:34.120
The only rule they agreed on was

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.883
that Mark Hornhat wasn't allowed.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.020
An initial scan of the room revealed

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.430
that nearly every table was already taken

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:45.620
with very few students
in line buying lunch.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:48.780
Maybe their plan wasn't
so original after all.

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:51.100
They walked around
methodically, not talking,

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:54.000
Rex doing his best to
play it cool and blend in,

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.240
not an easy task considering he towered

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:59.040
over almost everyone, while Leaf somehow

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.093
forgot to move his arms as he walked.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:04.530
After two and a half laps
around the cafeteria,

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:07.010
Rex looked at Leaf an
motioned with his head

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.950
toward a table next to them,

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:11.160
a handful of guys and
a girl they recognized

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:14.230
as upperclassmen were
deep in conversation.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:16.610
But there were three open seats.

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:19.450
Mind if we sit here, Rex asked.

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:22.930
Huh, a blonde girl with
a jean skirt asked.

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:25.580
Go for it stretch, a
guy with a Vanilla Ice

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:27.370
to the extreme T-shirt said

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:29.170
before turning back to jean skirt

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:31.120
and picking up where they had left off.

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:33.360
Thanks.

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:35.320
No sooner had Rex and Leaf sat down

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:38.920
that they got a powerful
whiff of eternity.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:41.540
Mark Hornhat appeared beside them

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.140
as of he'd been perched somewhere

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:45.460
waiting for them to decide on a table,

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:47.453
a very Hornhat move.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:50.660
Hey, hey fellas, he said,

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:52.770
taking his lunch out of his backpack.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.340
High school is pretty rocking, huh?

00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:58.030
So many hot babes.

00:21:58.030 --> 00:22:00.090
Rex and Leaf just started at him.

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:02.480
They both realized they
stood little chance

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:04.650
of repelling Hornhat.

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:08.513
Freshman lunch plan 1992
was quickly falling apart.

00:22:09.860 --> 00:22:12.560
Oh man he said, what y'all did at that

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.620
second Baptist fundraiser was so rad,

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:18.800
I can't wait to see Ghost
Dog so I can relive it.

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:21.200
Does Boikins have lunch this period?

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:23.460
I wanna congratulate
her on her performance.

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:26.320
Especially the part at the end, ha ha.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:27.970
Rex and Leaf continued starting,

00:22:27.970 --> 00:22:29.750
coming to grips with the fact that Hornhat

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:33.430
might be a permanent fixture
of their cafeteria crew.

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:35.830
Rex knew Hornhat's dad was a doctor,

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:38.280
so at least eating with
him on a regular basis

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:41.253
didn't guarantee a future as
an ice cream truck driver.

00:22:43.810 --> 00:22:47.470
First day of high school.

00:22:47.470 --> 00:22:52.470
When we conceptualized
the book we knew that

00:22:52.594 --> 00:22:57.594
we wanted sort of the
added tension and build up

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:04.180
that comes from the anxiety associated

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:05.520
with starting high school, right?

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:08.250
So that happens, you know, that is the end

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:10.176
of the summer of 1992,

00:23:10.176 --> 00:23:12.210
and these guys are getting
ready to go to high school,

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:13.810
and there's all these apprehensions,

00:23:13.810 --> 00:23:17.260
and of course, so I have
an older brother who,

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:19.330
when I was--
His name is not Misty.

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.750
His name is not Misty, it's Cole,

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:23.690
and he was a senior when I was a freshman.

00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:26.950
And so a lot of the
perceptions that you have

00:23:26.950 --> 00:23:29.540
about high school come
from your older siblings

